biography: Gradi Luakanda-Ndelemo is a bioinformatics scientist at the Institut National de Recherche Biomédicale (INRB) in Kinshasa, Democratic Republic of the Congo, where he has worked since 2021. His work focuses on genomic and phylogenetic analyses of high-priority pathogens, including mpox virus (MPXV), Ebola virus, and dengue virus, supporting outbreak investigations and genomic surveillance. He contributes to the analysis, curation, and interpretation of sequencing data for national and international collaborative studies. In parallel, he actively supports capacity building in public health genomics, serving as a facilitator in bioinformatics and sequencing training.
